# Line ends on checkout (step 116's restore drill: a fresh clone on a PC with core.autocrlf=true, Git for Windows'
# default, had every .sh outside twoc/tools/diag/sweep with CRLF). Shell scripts stay LF everywhere (bash outside
# Git Bash reads the CR as part of the line); batch files CRLF (cmd.exe can misread labels in LF files). Everything
# else follows core.autocrlf as before. twoc/tools/diag/sweep/.gitattributes says the same for its own scripts.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
